    <briefdescription>
<para>Check and read canopy input files (TXT or NETCDF) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This subroutine determines the input file format based on the file extension and validates it against the user-specified format option (infmt_opt). It then calls the appropriate reading routine:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>For .txt files: calls <ref refid="group__read__txt_1ga6cb9213adc871abc0d07476bfe3b3aba" kindref="member">canopy_read_txt()</ref></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>For .nc/.ncf/.nc4 files: calls <ref refid="namespacecanopy__ncf__io__mod_1a34fa94967d1a644cdde27c4484983673" kindref="member">canopy_read_ncf()</ref></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The subroutine performs error checking to ensure the file format matches the namelist specification and exits with an error code if there are mismatches.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">INFILE</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Primary input file path </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">INFILE2</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Secondary canopy profile input file path </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
